          "annotations": [],
          "text": "**Clinical Indication:**  \nHistory of combined generalized and focal epilepsy of immune etiology, with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at age 32 and occurring approximately once per month. The epilepsy is drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications are valproate and oxcarbazepine.\n\n**Technique:**  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG was performed using electrodes placed according to the International 10–20 system, with standard referential and bipolar montages.\n\n**Findings:**  \nEpileptiform abnormalities with both generalized and focal features are present. The focal abnormalities are not further localized in this report.\n\n**Impression:**  \nAbnormal routine EEG demonstrating combined generalized and focal epileptiform abnormalities. EEG findings alone do not establish the clinical seizure type or ictal onset localization.",
